  "facts": [
    "Åkrafjord Tunnel, 7,404 metres long, opened 15 July 2000, cutting through steep mountainsides to bypass a treacherous, winding fjord-side road, providing safer, faster travel for commuters and tourists alike.",
    "Located on European route E134, the tunnel sits southeast of Åkrafjorden, roughly fifteen kilometres northeast of the village of Etnesjøen, linking the region’s coastal and inland road networks.",
    "Since its inauguration, Åkrafjord Tunnel has dramatically reduced travel time across the fjord, eliminating the old narrow path that clung to the fjord’s steep cliffs and exposed drivers to hazardous conditions."
